Or on the upper river, or maybe on a wagon train to California.

01:19:04.370 --> 01:19:04.990
Excuse me.

01:19:08.680 --> 01:19:09.340
Hear what?

01:19:10.440 --> 01:19:10.780
Doot.

01:19:11.290 --> 01:19:11.550
Doot.

01:19:11.730 --> 01:19:11.910
Doot.

01:19:16.480 --> 01:19:16.560
Doot.

01:19:16.600 --> 01:19:16.760
Doot.

01:19:31.530 --> 01:19:31.770
Thank you.

01:20:02.430 --> 01:20:03.430
Am I out of my mind?

01:20:04.150 --> 01:20:05.530
How dare you worry us this way?

01:20:05.790 --> 01:20:07.920
I was never so mad at anyone in my life.

01:20:08.160 --> 01:20:09.460
Jeannie, how in the world did you get here?

01:20:09.820 --> 01:20:10.980
Never mind how I got here.

01:20:11.570 --> 01:20:12.370
How did you get here?

01:20:13.000 --> 01:20:14.080
Don't even drag the river.

01:20:14.240 --> 01:20:16.500
You have to break your leg.

01:20:17.140 --> 01:20:18.160
Sister, I'd be glad to.

01:20:18.340 --> 01:20:19.660
Oh, Jeannie, I've got to get you out of here.

01:20:19.700 --> 01:20:21.140
You're getting nobody, no folks.

01:20:21.180 --> 01:20:22.020
Oh, come on, Steve.

01:20:22.120 --> 01:20:23.920
Don't pay any attention to him, buttercup.

01:20:24.560 --> 01:20:25.860
Take your hand off me.

01:21:02.910 --> 01:21:21.020
Then stop trying to break up the peace and quiet unnatches.

01:21:31.630 --> 01:21:32.610
It's all right, Keeney.

01:21:48.300 --> 01:21:50.980
$50 advance royalties I squeezed out of old man Howard.

01:21:51.750 --> 01:21:52.370
Thanks, Dunning.

01:21:52.820 --> 01:21:55.160
Honestly, Steve, I never saw such luck in my life.

01:21:56.380 --> 01:21:56.960
Neither did I.

01:21:57.200 --> 01:21:59.620
Well, as soon as you get dressed, we'll go out and find you a northbound boat.

01:22:00.160 --> 01:22:01.320
Well, there's no hurry about it, Dunning.

01:22:01.630 --> 01:22:02.270
No hurry?

01:22:03.230 --> 01:22:05.790
Look, Steve, this letter from New York from the music publishers.

01:22:06.480 --> 01:22:07.720
That came the day you disappeared.

01:22:08.120 --> 01:22:09.120
Yeah, I know. You told me.

01:22:09.460 --> 01:22:10.880
Well, don't you see what it says there?

01:22:11.670 --> 01:22:12.610
I've read it, Dunning.

01:22:12.980 --> 01:22:14.360
Well, you saw what they're offering you.

01:22:14.850 --> 01:22:15.470
Oh, sure.

01:22:15.900 --> 01:22:16.540
Oh, sure?

01:22:17.120 --> 01:22:19.480
A deal like this won't lie around loose forever, you know.

01:22:22.160 --> 01:22:24.690
Dunning, I sort of thought that I'd like to...

01:22:24.690 --> 01:22:28.330
Do you realize what you'd have made out of old Susanna with a contract like these people want?

01:22:28.790 --> 01:22:29.970
Why, it would have run into...

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:59.000
thousands of dollars. I suppose. What's the matter with you, Steve? You afraid you can't write any more songs? You can at least sell the ones that Christy's singing now. Full of songs, all right. You're full of prunes, too, if you ask me. Suppose you only make up two songs a year. To guarantee you $500 a song, advance it as soon as you lay the darn tune on the line. You realize that's a cool thousand? Yeah, I know. And Christy pays you $50 a song for introducing them before publication. When I swear you ought to be paying him.

01:23:00.060 --> 01:23:02.700
You'll send the sails up like a pilot when the boiler busts.

01:23:02.740 --> 01:23:03.800
Dunning, it's only that I...

01:23:03.800 --> 01:23:06.800
How many folks in this country can lay hold of $1,000 all in one year?

01:23:07.590 --> 01:23:09.370
Oh, I'll think about it, Dunning, sure enough.

01:23:10.160 --> 01:23:10.880
Oh, you will.

01:23:11.800 --> 01:23:13.080
Might even know by tomorrow.

01:23:14.110 --> 01:23:16.070
Well, I'll be chawed and spit overboard.

01:23:16.430 --> 01:23:17.450
I purely will.

